    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45-a1">

                <pb facs="0152" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg64"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    331.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Errazuriz to
                        Mr. Egan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic">July 13,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In conformity with the indications which I
                    made to your excellency as soon as I entered, in June last, upon the duties of
                    the office which I hold, I have now the honor to communicate to your excellency
                    that my Government places at the disposition of your excellency the sum of
                    $75,000 gold, requesting that it may be distributed between the families of the
                    two seamen of the crew of the United States cruiser <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Baltimore</hi>, who died from wounds received in Valparaiso the 16th
                    October, 1891, and those of the crew of the same ship who may have suffered
                    personal injuries more or less grave from that lamentable occurrence.</p>
                <p>The undersigned would have been pleased to give effect before now to the offer
                    referred to, but he has had delay and embarrassment for want of exact knowledge
                    of the necessities to which the Government of Chile proposed to satisfy; and it
                    was for this reason that the undersigned permitted himself to indicate to your
                    excellency that the sum which he desired to place at your disposition should be
                    fixed by some high functionary of the United States who would find himself in a
                    better position to know the injuries caused to the persons and families of the
                    crew of the <hi rendition="#italic">Baltimore</hi> than we could be.</p>
                <p>I renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Isidoro
                    Errazuriz.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
